<article class="env-lemma" id="08NS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08NS">Lemma <span data-tag="08NS">14.30.8</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a trivial Kan fibration of simplicial sets. Then $f$ is a homotopy equivalence. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/08NM" data-tag="08NM">14.30.2</a> we can choose an right inverse $g : Y \to X$ to $f$. Consider the diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \partial \Delta [1] \times X \ar[d] \ar[r] &  X \ar[d] \\  \Delta [1] \times X \ar[r] \ar@{-->}[ru] &  Y }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Here the top horizontal arrow is given by $\text{id}_ X$ and $g \circ f$ where we use that $(\partial \Delta [1] \times X)_ n = X_ n \amalg X_ n$ for all $n \geq 0$. The bottom horizontal arrow is given by the map $\Delta [1] \to \Delta [0]$ and $f : X \to Y$. The diagram commutes as $f \circ g \circ f = f$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/08NM" data-tag="08NM">14.30.2</a> we can fill in the dotted arrow and we win. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>